\n\n- Reproducible in versions after 4.4.dev4 .Net.\n- Not reproducible in earlier versions.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot v4.4.rc2 .Net - Mobile - Nvidia GeForce RTX 2080\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running my game it generates a number of:   \nERROR: Script class can only be set together with base class name.\nERROR: Script class can only be set together with base class name\n\nThe number of errors changes and I cannot figure out what causes the errors.  There is no indication in the inspector what is causing these errors.  Its seems like they are often divisible by 8.  So sometimes 8, and sometimes 32 etc.  I believe they are two different errors since one has a period at the end and the other doesn't.  It didn't throw these errors when I was on Godot v4.4.dev4 and if I roll back the to that version it also doesn't throw the errors.  \n\nThe errors don't seem to cause any issues, though and the game runs fine.\n\nI assume I am just doing something wrong in my code, but no one seems to have any idea about why it would happen or even where to start looking to solve it.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI cannot reproduce it in any of my other projects.  I can include a link to my project, but it is pretty big.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI really wish I could include a MRP because then I could have narrowed down what is causing the issue.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscrip